Algorithm
Start the program.
Read the number of vertices and edges.
Create an adjacency list to represent the graph.
Read the edges connecting the vertices.
Accept the starting vertex from the user.
Initialize all vertices as unvisited and their levels as -1.
Insert the starting vertex into the queue and mark it as visited.
Remove a vertex from the queue and display it.
Visit all its unvisited adjacent vertices, mark them as visited, assign their BFS levels, and insert them into the queue.
Repeat Steps 8–9 until the queue becomes empty.
Display the BFS traversal order.
Display all reachable and unvisited vertices.
Count and display the number of reachable vertices.
Display the BFS level of each reachable vertex.
Stop the program.
